WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.554
Picture the classic car lot. You argue. The salesperson

2
00:00:03.554 --> 00:00:06.583
goes to check with the manager. You argue some more.

3
00:00:06.863 --> 00:00:09.135
Two hours later, you're not even sure who won.

4
00:00:10.085 --> 00:00:12.959
CarMax flipped that script with a one-price policy.

5
00:00:13.239 --> 00:00:16.988
The sticker price is the price, for every single buyer. No haggling.

6
00:00:17.938 --> 00:00:22.240
That's the opposite of dynamic pricing, where the price changes depending

7
00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:26.128
on the buyer and the situation, like surge fares or airline seats.

8
00:00:27.078 --> 00:00:30.992
One-price policies feel fair and simple, and they save a lot of time.

9
00:00:31.272 --> 00:00:35.355
The trade-off? Skilled negotiators lose their chance to score a better deal.

10
00:00:36.305 --> 00:00:39.546
Your turn. Would you rather haggle, or just see one fair price?

11
00:00:39.826 --> 00:00:41.868
Explain who wins with each policy.
